※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5003 LANG_FUNCDEF_RETURN_MISSING

※ A semicolon separates and never terminates, so a body ending in one ends in
※ a statement that is empty -- and an empty statement produces no value, so a
※ function declared to answer with one has not answered.
@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    @[ignore(5005)]
    7u8;
